          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text fields keep standard macOS editing keys. Dialogs share the Apply/Cancel assignments above. Numeric fields use Up/Down, with Shift for larger steps. Standard macOS commands include ⌘Q to quit and ⌃⌘F for full screen. The shortcut editor itself always uses Return to save and Esc to cancel when not recording.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Text fields keep standard macOS editing keys. Dialogs share the Apply/Cancel assignments above. Numeric fields use Up/Down, with Shift for larger steps. Standard macOS commands include ⌘Q to quit and ⌃⌘F for full screen. The shortcut editor itself always uses Return to save and Esc to cancel when not recording."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les champs de texte conservent les touches d’édition standard de macOS. Les dialogues partagent les raccourcis Appliquer et Annuler ci-dessus. Les champs numériques utilisent Haut et Bas, et Maj pour de plus grands pas. Les commandes macOS standard incluent ⌘Q pour quitter et ⌃⌘F pour le plein écran. L’éditeur de raccourcis utilise toujours Retour pour enregistrer et Esc pour annuler, tant qu’il n’enregistre pas un raccourci."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That selection is too detailed to outline. Try a different Tolerance, or turn on Contiguous.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "That selection is too detailed to outline. Try a different Tolerance, or turn on Contiguous."
